      "description": {
        "type": "/type/text",
        "value": "A Roberts reissue of Louisa May Alcott’s Civil War collection, this volume pairs *Hospital Sketches*, her semi-autobiographical account of nursing wounded Union soldiers at Georgetown’s Union Hotel Hospital during the winter of 1862–63, with twelve short stories set during and after the war. Combining humor, pathos, social criticism, and firsthand observation, Alcott examines military hospital life, abolition, loyalty, bereavement, romance, and the war’s lasting effects on soldiers and civilians alike."
      },
